// ActivateChangeRequest invokes activateChangeRequest operation.
//
// Creates and activates a new configuration version from an approved change request; each context
// applies its part. Human-only. Requires status `approved`; a change of validation rules also needs a
// passed simulation of this exact proposal (409 `config.rules_not_simulated`). The ledger checks the
// controlling rules again against its data, which may have changed since submission (a default cost or
// profit center no longer usable, postings in the year a center accounting switch turns on, a removed
// cost center category in use): 409 `ledger.controlling_invalid`, naming each finding (ADR-0050 §4).
// A tax registration whose company, group, authority, number, return type, frequency or first period
// changed under its code since submission is refused: 409 `tax.registration_fixed` (ADR-0049 §10).
// While replicas of several versions run (a rolling upgrade), a proposal setting a key that a running
// replica's version does not know, which it would ignore (a company's `release_dual_limit`), is
// refused: 409 `config.replica_lacks_key`, each such key in `errors` (`field` the key's path, e.g.
// `companies[].release_dual_limit`, and the versions lacking it in `message`); activate it once every
// replica runs a version that knows the key (ADR-0038). An account flagged `asset_reconciliation` that
// the chart already has is refused (409 `ledger.asset_reconciliation_not_new`, ADR-0057): only a new
// account becomes an asset reconciliation account. An existing account whose cost element becomes
// `secondary`, or a secondary cost element given another cost element, is refused (409
// `ledger.secondary_account_not_new`, ADR-0064 §4): an account is a secondary cost element from its
// creation and stays one. An account determination key the proposal no longer names is removed (a key
// with a fallback, such as `cash_discount_granted`, posts to the fallback's account again), but for
