// `sales.item_repeated`) takes the quantity given, in its own unit (422 `sales.unit_mismatch`), and
// the unit price given, in the order's currency, with its price unit; what is not given stays. A
// changed item is checked and priced again as an item given directly is (`createSalesOrder`), on the
// order's date: an entered price stays entered, an item priced from the price records takes the record
// valid on that date again, with the pricing procedure's discounts; its account, tax code and tax
// jurisdiction, which stay, are checked again on that date (422 `sales.account_not_postable`,
// `sales.unknown_tax_code`, `sales.tax_jurisdiction_required`, `sales.tax_jurisdiction_not_levied`).
// An item's quantity is never below what is delivered of it (422 `sales.quantity_below_delivered`
// naming `items[i].quantity.value`), and an item of which something is billed keeps its quantity and
// price (422 `sales.order_item_billed` naming `items[i]`): cancel the billing document first
// (`cancelBillingDocument`). A confirmed order's revenue contract (`getRevenueContract`) follows the
// change by itself, shortly after it (ADR-0068, As built T81e). `requested_delivery_date` is on or
// after the order's date (422 `sales.invalid_requested_delivery_date`); `null` clears it. From T78e a
// change also adds items (`new_items`), removes items with nothing delivered (`removed_items`) and
// changes the payment term while nothing of the order is billed (`payment_term_code`); a removed item
// is not changed again (422 `sales.order_item_removed`). A request that changes nothing is refused
// (422 `sales.nothing_changed`). The order's net value is the sum of its items' that stand again. A
// change that raises a confirmed order's net value checks the customer's credit for the increase, as a
// confirmation checks the order (`confirmSalesOrder`): an order that no longer fits the limit is
// blocked again (`credit_block` `blocked`, published as SalesOrderCreditBlocked), whatever an earlier
// release; a lower value leaves the block as it is. A confirmed order without a plant takes no item of
// a material kept in stock that the change adds or whose quantity it changes (422
// `sales.plant_required` naming `plant_id`; product owner 2026-11-21): its availability could not be
// checked. A confirmed order with a plant has the items the change adds, and those whose quantity it
// changes, checked for availability again as a confirmation checks them (`confirmSalesOrder`, S2j): an
// item keeps what it had confirmed, up to its new quantity, and has more confirmed as far as the plant
// has it available, or in full on the material's replenishment lead time when the order, as changed,
// asks for delivery on or after the company's date today plus that lead time (S2j2). The change is
