// CreateMaterialDocument invokes createMaterialDocument operation.
//
// Posts a goods movement of one movement type (ADR-0082 §7, S1c) as a material document: `501` a
// receipt without a purchase order, `561` an initial entry of stock, `201` an issue to a cost center,
// `551` a scrapping, `311` a transfer between storage locations of a plant, `301` a transfer between
// plants of one company; each item moves a quantity of a material at a plant's storage location. Each
// material is an `active` material (422 `inventory.material_invalid` when there is none with the id,
// `inventory.material_not_usable` when it is pending or blocked) kept in stock, so neither of type
// `non_stock` nor `service` (422 `inventory.material_not_stocked`); each plant an active plant of a
// company the caller may act in (422 `inventory.plant_invalid`) that the material is extended to (422
// `inventory.plant_not_extended`), each storage location an active one under it (422
// `inventory.storage_location_invalid`) the material is kept at (422
// `inventory.storage_location_not_extended`), and every plant of the document one company's (422
// `inventory.mixed_companies`). The quantity is positive (422 `inventory.invalid_quantity`), in the
// material's base unit or one of its alternative units (422 `inventory.unknown_unit`), and converted
// exactly to the base unit, never rounded (422 `inventory.inexact_quantity`). A `201` or `551` names a
// cost center (422 `inventory.cost_center_required`), an active one of the company in force on the
// posting date (422 `inventory.cost_center_invalid`); another movement type names none (422
// `inventory.cost_center_not_allowed`). A `311` names the storage location received at, under the same
// plant (`to_storage_location_id`); a `301` the plant and storage location received at (`to_plant_id`,
// `to_storage_location_id`), another plant of the company; each is checked as the issuing one is (422
// `inventory.transfer_target_required`, `inventory.same_location`); another movement type names
// neither (422 `inventory.transfer_not_allowed`). The reversal types (`502`, `562`, `202`, `552`,
// `312`, `302`) are posted by `reverseMaterialDocument` only, a purchase order's goods receipt (`101`)
// by `postGoodsReceipt`, an outbound delivery's goods issue (`601`) by
// `postOutboundDeliveryGoodsIssue`, a stock transport order's goods issue (`351`) by
// `postStockTransportGoodsIssue` and a count's differences (`701`, `702`) by
// `postPhysicalInventoryDifferences` (422 `inventory.unknown_movement_type`). The document is posted
// on the company's date today in its time zone and numbered from its `material_document` range of that
// date's fiscal year (422 `ledger.no_fiscal_period` when the date is in none, `config.no_number_range`
// when the range is missing). Stock never goes below zero: an issue of more than a storage location
// holds is refused naming the material, the location and both quantities (409
// `inventory.insufficient_stock`), and two issues of the last quantity at once post one; a stock that
// would exceed 14 integer digits is refused (422 `inventory.quantity_too_large`). Each item is one
// line in the base unit, signed (a receipt positive, an issue negative); a transfer's item is two, the
// issue and the receipt. The lines are applied in order, and each leaves its location's stock at zero
// or more, so items that move stock round a circle out of an empty location are refused though they
// change nothing in all. A material at a storage location an open physical inventory count document
// counts is not moved there (409 `inventory.posting_blocked`, naming the document; S2c). A
// batch-managed material's item names a batch of it (`batch_id`, S2f; 422 `inventory.batch_required`,
// `inventory.batch_invalid`), another material's none (422 `inventory.batch_not_allowed`); a transfer
// receives the same batch, and a batch's stock at a location never goes below zero either (409
// `inventory.insufficient_stock`, naming the batch), so a location's batches add up to its stock. A
// serial-managed material's item names the serial number of each unit it moves (`serial_numbers`,
// S2g): as many as its quantity in base units, a whole number (422 `inventory.serial_required`,
// `inventory.serial_quantity`), each once in the document (422 `inventory.serial_repeated`), and
// another material's none (422 `inventory.serial_not_allowed`); a receipt's serial numbers are in no
// stock, a new one created by it (409 `inventory.serial_in_stock`, naming it), an issue's in stock at
// the item's storage location (409 `inventory.serial_not_in_stock`), a transfer receives the same
// serial numbers and a reversal moves its original's back, so a serial number is in stock at most once
// (`GET /v1/serial-numbers`). Every line is valued (S1d): its material is valued in its plant (422
// `inventory.no_valuation`; `createMaterialValuation`), an issue takes the value the stock leaves (at
// a standard price the rest is worth its quantity at the price; at a moving price the value in
// proportion, so issuing the whole stock takes its whole value), a receipt adds what it is worth
// (`amount`, only on a `501` or `561`, 422 `inventory.amount_not_allowed`, in the company's currency,
// 422 `inventory.currency_mismatch`; else its quantity at the moving price, 422 `inventory.no_price`
// while that is zero; at a standard price what the stock is worth at it after the receipt, the rest a
// price difference), a transfer's receipt what its issue took. The value is posted through the ledger
// in one journal entry dated the posting date (document type `WE` for a receipt or initial entry, `WA`
// otherwise; none when the document moves no value): the valuation class's stock account against the
// account its movement type posts to (receipt, initial entry, consumption with the item's cost center,
// scrapping), and price differences on its price difference account (422
// `inventory.no_inventory_account` when the class lacks an account, and the ledger's refusals, such as
// 422 `ledger.period_not_open`); a refused posting moves nothing. Audited, and published as
// MaterialDocumentPosted. A retry with the same `Idempotency-Key` answers the document posted.
// Human-only (`x-agent: false`).
//
// POST /v1/material-documents
