// GetLiquidityForecast invokes getLiquidityForecast operation.
//
// The liquidity forecast of a legal entity (ADR-0051 §9, T53e), computed at the read from one
// database state (a repeatable-read snapshot): the flows expected from the read date (the company's
// date in its configured time zone, shown as `time_zone`) in the company's buckets (`cash.buckets`;
// default 14 days, 11 weeks and 9 months: each grain's periods follow the previous grain's, a week
// being seven days and a month running to the same day of the next month, its last day when shorter),
// per currency, never converted. Flows: `payable` (`expected`), the posted supplier open items (not
// special G/L items such as down payments) that no live payment run holds, each expected when a
// payment run would pay it (ADR-0051 §5, P5): while the company takes cash discounts
// (`cash.take_discounts`, default true), the last day of the earliest discount tier still open, else
// the net due date (by the terms the item was posted with, else its supplier's net days; a credit
// memo's is its document date), moved back to the company's last payment day (`cash.payment_days`;
// none: any day) on or before it but not before the read date (a tier that would be is passed over for
// the next, or the net due date), an overdue item on the next payment day; then the value days
// (`cash.value_days`) of the house bank the supplier's first payment method ranks for the item's
// currency, moved to the next working day of the company's calendar (weekends and its holidays). Its
// amount is what a run on that payment day pays: what the item owes less the cash discount it then
// takes and the withholding tax deducted at payment, as the proposer computes them (one rule,
// `ledger.ItemTerms`), netted per supplier and currency as a run nets them: one flow per supplier
// payment; a day whose items owe nothing net pays nothing and its items are carried to the supplier's
// next payment day, and a debit balance left after the last is no flow. `payment_run` (`confirmed`),
// the payments of runs `proposed` or `releasing` not posted yet, whose items they hold, on their run
// date plus their bank's value days moved to the next working day, `late` when that is before the read
// date (then expected the working day after it), as in the cash position. `invoice_unposted`
// (`planned`, T53e2), the supplier invoices, credit memos and subsequent debits and credits `parked`
// or `on_hold`, which are no open items yet: each at what it would be owed posted now, by the payment
// terms and withholding tax codes it would post with (its order's term, else its supplier's, from its
// invoice date; a correction naming an invoice that invoice's terms; a credit memo none), expected by
// the same rule as `payable` and netted per supplier and currency among themselves (not with the
// posted items, which are more certain); what would refuse its posting does not refuse the forecast: a
// term not configured gives way to its supplier's net days, and withholding tax codes that would
// refuse it are left out. `down_payment` (`expected`, T53e2), the open down payment requests that no
// live run pays, each whole and never netted (a run pays a request on its own), on its due date moved
// to the next working day, `late` when that is before the read date. `purchase_order` (`planned`,
// T53g), the open value of the released purchase orders: each item's ordered quantity less what its
// supplier documents posted, parked or on hold invoice (net of credit memos, with what the source
// system invoiced before migration), at its price, plus the tax its tax code gives on the read date
// (the tax the supplier charges, as an invoice's is calculated, per code; a code that cannot be
// calculated then adds none), less the order's down payment requests not yet cleared (open ones are
// `down_payment` flows of their own), taken from its earliest invoices first; its invoice is expected
// on the item's `delivery_date`, else the order date plus the company's `cash.order_lead_days`
// (default 30), and paid by the order's payment terms from that day (a term not configured: its
// supplier's net days) by the same rule as `payable`, an order's items expected on one day being one
// document; closed, cancelled, draft or fully invoiced orders add nothing; netted per supplier and
// currency among themselves. A supplier blocked for payment or posting, inactive, or not set up in the
// company is paid by no run: its items, unposted invoices, requests and open orders are
// `payable_blocked` (each keeping its own certainty), on their net due date (a request's due date; an
// overdue one on the read date), at what they owe then, netted as a run would, apart from the totals:
// listed in each bucket's flows and summed per currency in `blocked`, but counted in the buckets'
// `total`s, the currency's `total` and `beyond` only with `include_blocked=true`. Amounts are signed:
// a payment out is negative. Each currency gives its flows per bucket by source, certainty and
// lateness with the bucket's total, the total over the horizon, and what is expected after the last
// bucket (`beyond`, in no bucket). Each currency also gives its rows by liquidity item and its
// hierarchy (`items`, T53e3; ADR-0051 §4, §9): every flow is split over the liquidity items
// (`cash.liquidity_items`) its documents derive by the configuration's `cash.derivation`: a supplier
// payment over the documents it pays, each at what the payment pays of it, and each document over its
// offsetting lines (a posted item's expense, asset and tax lines, an unposted invoice's items; never
// the supplier's line nor a withholding tax withheld at invoice), in proportion to their signed
// amounts, a line taking the item of the first account rule covering its account, else its supplier's
// planning group's, else the default of the flow's direction; a tax line follows the base lines of its
// tax code in proportion to their amounts, and a self-assessed pair (`self_output`/`self_input` of a
// reverse charge or import code), which moves no cash, is left out before the split. A down payment
// request, and a run's payment of one, has no lines and takes its supplier's planning group's item or
// the default. Each split rounds once to minor units by largest remainder (ties to the item named
// first), so an item's shares add up to the flow. Each row gives the item's code, name, parent and
// level, its flows and its descendants' per bucket (`buckets`, in the forecast's buckets' order), over
// the horizon (`total`) and after the last bucket (`beyond`), counted as the buckets' totals count
// them, so the top rows add up to each bucket's `total`, and the item's own flows by source and
// certainty; a row without `liquidity_item` holds what no rule assigns and no default covers.
// `min_certainty` cuts the less certain flows (actual, confirmed, expected, planned; default planned,
// every flow). T53e4 adds two sources, the opening position, one grain over a range, conversion and
// drill-down. `in_transit` (`confirmed`): the payments released from the company's active house banks
// whose line on the bank's clearing account is still open and that no statement line up to the bank's
// opening statement matches, as in the cash position (`getCashPosition`), on their run date plus the
// bank's value days moved to the next working day, `late` before the read date. `memo`: the `active`
// memo records of the legal entity, with or without a house bank, at their own certainty and liquidity
// item, each on its value date moved to the next working day (`late` before the read date) and not
